From 14799c906344d7ac0e923aeaa5ad99bc63fffb13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neimar Avila <neimar.avila@vsgroup.com.br>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:49:29 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(relay): handle DeepSeek V4 streaming edge cases in
 OpenAI->Claude

Upstream PR #6629 (PengJunchen), reconciled onto PR #6394, which we also
carry. Both rewrite the same OpenAI->Claude stream lifecycle, so two hunks
could not be taken verbatim:

- convmeta/meta.go: #6394 appends ToolCallOpenIndexes to the same struct
  tail where #6629 appends HasContentBlock. Both fields are kept.
- to_claude_messages_resp.go: `state.HasContentBlock = true` on the
  tool-call branch is re-anchored after #6394's ToolCallOpenIndexes
  initialisation.

Everything else applies unchanged, and the two fixes turn out to be
orthogonal: appendEmptyTextFallback only runs when neither a text nor a
tool_use block was ever emitted, so LastMessagesType is None or Thinking
on that path and #6394's rewritten LastMessageTypeTools branch of
stopOpenBlocks is unreachable there.

To refresh: apply the patches sorting before this one, run
`patch -p1 < 6629.patch` from GitHub, re-anchor the two rejects, and
regenerate. Acceptance is both PRs' tests green together:
`cd relaykit && GOWORK=off go test -count=1 ./relayconvert/internal/oai_chat/`
